  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Kept the Western 12-hour count: Tigrinya is split between Ethiopia (Ethiopian time) and Eritrea (Western clock in everyday/official use); one locale cannot serve both and rotating hours would be wrong for every Eritrean speaker and for digital-clock readers. Phrases use the -ን…-ን coordination ('ሰለስተን ፈረቓን' half past three, 'ሰለስተን ርብዒን' quarter past), ':00' = '{h} ሰዓት', and 'ጎደል' (less) for :40-:55 with {next_h} ('ርብዒ ጎደል ኣርባዕተ'). :35 kept additive ('…ን ሰላሳን ሓሙሽተን'). Doubts: ርብዒ+ን spelled ርብዒን (vs ርብዕን); 'ጎደል' vs the Amharic-influenced 'ጉዳይ'."
    }
  ]
